{
  "course": "初中60短文",
  "passage": 47,
  "title": "Passage 47",
  "voice": "温暖自然英式女老师｜IndexTTS2.5 慢速教学",
  "sentences": [
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 1,
      "sourceSentenceId": 1,
      "chunkId": "s47-p01",
      "image": "assets/images/01.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p01.mp3",
      "en": "Squirrels are cute and interesting animals that can be found in many parts of the world.",
      "cn": "松鼠是一种可爱又有趣的动物，分布在世界许多地方。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 2,
      "sourceSentenceId": 2,
      "chunkId": "s47-p02",
      "image": "assets/images/02.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p02.mp3",
      "en": "They are known for their long tails, big teeth and the ability to climb trees.",
      "cn": "它们以长尾巴、大牙齿和爬树的本领而闻名。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 3,
      "sourceSentenceId": 3,
      "chunkId": "s47-p03",
      "image": "assets/images/03.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p03.mp3",
      "en": "They can jump up to about 3 metres in height, and they can run up to about 30 kilometres every hour.",
      "cn": "它们能跳到约3米高，每小时能跑约30公里。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 4,
      "sourceSentenceId": 4,
      "chunkId": "s47-p04",
      "image": "assets/images/04.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p04.mp3",
      "en": "Squirrels have soft bodies.",
      "cn": "松鼠的身体柔软。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 5,
      "sourceSentenceId": 5,
      "chunkId": "s47-p05-01",
      "image": "assets/images/05.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p05-01.mp3",
      "en": "Their eyes are high on their small heads and are placed on each side,",
      "cn": "它们的眼睛长在小脑袋上较高的位置，每侧各有一只，因此它们无需转身就能看得又广又远。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 6,
      "sourceSentenceId": 5,
      "chunkId": "s47-p05-02",
      "image": "assets/images/05.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p05-02.mp3",
      "en": "so they can see wide and far without having to turn around.",
      "cn": "它们的眼睛长在小脑袋上较高的位置，每侧各有一只，因此它们无需转身就能看得又广又远。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 7,
      "sourceSentenceId": 6,
      "chunkId": "s47-p06",
      "image": "assets/images/06.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p06.mp3",
      "en": "This often helps them get out of danger from their enemies like foxes and wolves.",
      "cn": "这往往能帮助它们躲避来自狐狸和狼等敌人的危险。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 8,
      "sourceSentenceId": 7,
      "chunkId": "s47-p07",
      "image": "assets/images/07.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p07.mp3",
      "en": "Squirrels have four big teeth in the front of their mouth that keep growing all through their lives.",
      "cn": "松鼠的嘴前方有四颗大牙齿，这些牙齿会终生不断生长。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 9,
      "sourceSentenceId": 8,
      "chunkId": "s47-p08-01",
      "image": "assets/images/08.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p08-01.mp3",
      "en": "They are known for their love of nuts,",
      "cn": "它们以爱吃坚果而闻名，"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 10,
      "sourceSentenceId": 8,
      "chunkId": "s47-p08-02",
      "image": "assets/images/08.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p08-02.mp3",
      "en": "and they can eat as much food as their body weight each week.",
      "cn": "每周能吃下相当于自己体重的食物量。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 11,
      "sourceSentenceId": 9,
      "chunkId": "s47-p09",
      "image": "assets/images/09.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p09.mp3",
      "en": "They often keep nuts in the ground for the long winter months.",
      "cn": "它们经常把坚果藏在地里，以备漫长的冬季之需。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 12,
      "sourceSentenceId": 10,
      "chunkId": "s47-p10",
      "image": "assets/images/10.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p10.mp3",
      "en": "Many people think that squirrels only eat nuts, but this isn't true.",
      "cn": "很多人认为松鼠只吃坚果，其实不然。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 13,
      "sourceSentenceId": 11,
      "chunkId": "s47-p11",
      "image": "assets/images/11.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p11.mp3",
      "en": "Their diet also includes plants, fruits, eggs, small animals and even young snakes.",
      "cn": "它们的日常饮食还包括植物、水果、蛋类、小动物，甚至小蛇。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 14,
      "sourceSentenceId": 12,
      "chunkId": "s47-p12",
      "image": "assets/images/12.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p12.mp3",
      "en": "One funny thing is that squirrels are good at planting trees.",
      "cn": "有趣的是，松鼠擅长种树。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 15,
      "sourceSentenceId": 13,
      "chunkId": "s47-p13",
      "image": "assets/images/13.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p13.mp3",
      "en": "They hide the fruits of oak trees in the soil, but often forget where they put them.",
      "cn": "它们会把橡树的果实藏在土里，但又经常忘记放在了哪个地方。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 16,
      "sourceSentenceId": 14,
      "chunkId": "s47-p14",
      "image": "assets/images/14.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p14.mp3",
      "en": "In the end, the forgotten fruits become big trees.",
      "cn": "最后，这些被遗忘的果实就会长成大树。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 17,
      "sourceSentenceId": 15,
      "chunkId": "s47-p15",
      "image": "assets/images/15.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p15.mp3",
      "en": "Sometimes we even find them in our yards.",
      "cn": "有时，我们甚至会在自家院子里发现它们。"
    }
  ],
